ons - argv/env_literals/task_element_id are declared in BYTES and implemented in bytes, media_type/symlink target/logical_id/goal_id/repository_identity/tree_identity/remote name are declared in CHARACTERS and accept multibyte values exactly at the bound; Sections 10.2-10.4 member sets, kind invariants, sparse pairing, submodule depth/count/acyclicity, gitlink binding and TM-GIT-N2 all match the pinned tables; accepted-leaf scalar content is byte-identical to the checkpoint tarball. Reviewer re-ran build, vet, go test ./... (8 packages ok), tracecheck -section 17.3 (assigned_scopes=1) and all four fuzz targets at 100x - all exit 0; race/cover/gofmt/cataloggen/cross-builds accepted from the rev7 validation log. REWORK METHOD: do not add only a name regex. Five rounds have each fixed exactly the named field and been defeated by the next unenumerated one. Apply the structural fix at the FIELD level the way it was applied at the registry level: the enumeration artifact must carry one row per declared member of every completely-validated schema, each naming its enforcing call site, with an explicit quoted row for members that genuinely carry no constraint beyond their type, preferably derived from the requireExactMembers argument lists so artifact and code cannot drift. Then fix F2 and F3. Evidence: TASK-260830-8x76g1_review-verdict-rev7.md, TASK-260830-8x76g1_review-evidence-rev7.tar.gz. Working tree verified byte-identical to candidate tree 2101a33011a27c98903679163545a7a778027b07 before and after every probe and mutant.\nagent completed: [reviewer] reviewer (claude) (exit=0)\nspawn run completed: claude (run=RUN-260831-a35299, pid=35903, exit=0)\nCR revision 7 reviewed by claude/opus after the codex reviewer was blocked four consecutive times by the provider content filter. The switch paid off immediately: F3 is a measured CPU-amplification defect no earlier round found. validateManifestEntries compares each path against every earlier one with strings.EqualFold, which